# Testing

- Keep tests under `tests/`; never ship test-only dependencies in production projects.
- Prefer deterministic unit tests; mark lab/integration cases skippable when external systems are unavailable.
- Do not weaken assertions or raise arbitrary timeouts to hide races—fix the race or wait for the real invariant.
- Do not disable parallelization globally without evidence of shared mutable state.
- Report exact pass/fail/skip counts; distinguish a failed full run from a passing isolated rerun.
- Integration tests bind loopback listeners on port 0 and must dispose every host, server, socket and client they create, including on failure, cancellation and timeout (`try/finally` or `await using`).
- FFmpeg interoperability tests skip only when FFmpeg/ffprobe are absent and `RTSP_FFMPEG_REQUIRED` is not `true`; CI sets it so a missing tool fails the run. Locally, `RTSP_FFMPEG_PATH` selects the FFmpeg binary.
- Process-wide measurements (`GC.GetTotalMemory`, working set) are only meaningful with no concurrent tests: place them in a `DisableParallelization` collection.
